  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nIsolated showers continue to move onshore this afternoon as moisture \nand some mid-level energy move toward the coast. Expect the coverage \nwill increase as the seabreeze moves inland. It is still unclear how \nfar inland showers and thunderstorms will make it this afternoon and \nMonday. By Tuesday, high pressure will rebuild over the area, \nsettling in and limiting rain chances through the rest of the week.\n\nTemperatures remain generally around seasonal averages, but will \nrange from a degree or two below normal Sunday to a few degrees \nabove normal by late in the work week. Heat index values increase \nfor the latter half of the period and heat advisories may become \nnecessary by mid-week.",
